Prompt:

Theme: {THEME}
Title: {TITLE}
Subtitle: {SUBTITLE}
Key visual material: {VISUAL SYSTEM}
Focal object: {OBJECT}
Main color: {COLOR}
Information: {DATE / LOCATION / DATA}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a refined vertical editorial poster with a contemporary Japanese museum-publication aesthetic.

Use a continuous warm ivory paper background, subtle print texture and a low-saturation palette.

Place one complete oversized circular visual field in the upper-left area with comfortable margins. Translate the theme into meaningful internal textures such as rings, grids, waveforms, material layers or measurement structures.

Build 5–6 secondary circles, partial discs and open rings below it with strong scale variation and controlled overlap.

Connect the composition with extremely fine theme-specific lines.

Place one small concrete theme-related object near the lower-left corner.

Use a large elegant English serif title on the right in two or three horizontal lines, with a much smaller subtitle. Put authentic small project information and technical data on the left.

Keep strong contrast between large and small, dense and empty, abstract and concrete.

Maintain the same paper, typography, line weight, information density and layout logic across a series, while changing subject, colors and materials.

No cropped main circle, no separate right-side white strip, no 3D, no glossy commercial look, no neon, no sparkles, no numbering, no watermark, no meaningless placeholder text.

Anything, including manga characters, can be turned edible with a prompt like this.

do this for 4 famous manga, 2x2 grid, 16:9 A = { main silhouette: the subject’s recognizable outer shape, preserved }
B = { internal zones: functional rooms or sections, inferred from subject }
C = { symbolic props: tiny story-telling objects made from food }
D = { tiny figures: rice-and-nori people or edible characters }
E = { food materials: sushi rice, sashimi slabs, tamago, nori, roe, garnish }
F = { plate and ground: black ceramic plate, sushi rice terrain, sesame scatter }
G = { lighting/camera: dark premium food photo, macro shallow DOF }

DIORAMA = (A ∩ silhouette_lock) ∪ (B ∩ cutaway_scenes) ∪ (C ∩ props) ∪ (D ∩ actors) ∪ (E ∩ material_map) ∪ (F ∩ base) ∪ (G ∩ atmosphere)

Rules:
- A is built from pressed rice blocks, sashimi slabs, tamago panels.
- B uses nori strips, cucumber rods, chive beams for thin supports.
- C uses tobiko, sesame, roe, wasabi, pickled garnish.
- D are tiny edible figures performing inferred actions.
- G gives glossy fish highlights, sticky rice grain detail, matte nori texture.
- No random ingredient clutter; every element serves the diorama.
Output: single luxury food diorama image, 8K.

